# Component Repository Mode (Cursor Component Factory)

Follow:
- `fast-workflow/CORE_WORKFLOW.md`;
- `fast-workflow/COMPONENT_REPO_WORKFLOW.md`.

Before editing, identify:
- Component passport: `COMPONENT.md`;
- Feature specification: `product/features/<feature>.md`;
- Approved two-tier contracts: Protocol Contract (`contracts/protocol/` or `contracts/front/`) and Domain Capability Contract (`contracts/domain/`);
- Paired in-repo mock suite (`mocks/`);
- Allowed paths: current component repository root;
- Required checks (happy path, validation error, dependency failure, rollback on failed parameter, empty result).

## Scope & Boundaries

- Modify only the current component repository.
- Work toward a reproducible `Ready` version.
- Use **Two-Tier Contracts & Zero-Manual Mocks**: develop domain contracts strictly in pair with an in-repo mock suite (`mocks/`), providing auto-generated mock servers (Prism, MSW, WireMock) or fixtures (Faker+Zod, Polyfactory, FastAPI/Pydantic mock classes, YAxUnit mocks) directly from the contract schema.
- Keep external repositories completely unchanged.

## 1C:Enterprise Specifics (if applicable)

- Source code must be stored in text format (1C:EDT or XML/BSL export).
- Unit tests and mocks: `YAxUnit` (`tests/unit/`).
- BDD scenarios: `Vanessa-Automation` (`tests/scenarios/*.feature`).
- Build artifacts: `.cfe` or `.cf` compiled in CI and attached to Git Tag.

## Stop Conditions

Stop and report when:
- An approved contract schema must change (requires human approval and SemVer update);
- Required business behavior is ambiguous (record in Open Questions);
- A required change belongs to another component or service;
- An auto-mock cannot represent the published contract.

Do not claim `Integrated` in this mode. When marking a version `Ready`, synchronously update `COMPONENT.md` and `README.md` (version, status, changelog of the latest release, run and test instructions). After editing, run local checks (success + failure) and report evidence, assumptions, questions, and risks.
